  <prompt>
    Two coupled deliverables completing thread regarding-resolution + naming (FR-07, building on the FR-06 schema from task 002):

    **(1) Naming re-derive (BFF).** Add "re-derive `sprk_name` UNLESS user-edited" logic to `ThreadResolver.BuildTopic()` (`src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/ThreadResolver.cs` ~line 175), gated by the **naming-edited marker** field added in task 002. Today `BuildTopic` runs ONCE at thread create (`sprk_name` line 101) and is never revisited; `sprk_name` is user-editable but a later regarding change never refreshes it. FR-07: when a thread's regarding changes AND the marker says "auto", re-run `BuildTopic` and update `sprk_name`; when the marker says "edited" (a user changed the name), preserve the user's name on subsequent regarding changes. The marker flips to "edited" on user edit.

    **(2) RegardingResolver PCF on the thread form (0 code).** Place the EXISTING entity-agnostic RegardingResolver PCF (`src/client/pcf/RegardingResolver/`, FR-22 — attaches to any form via its `entity` prop, **zero code change**) on the `sprk_communicationthread` main form with `entity="sprk_communicationthread"`, binding the **new Lookup discriminator** field added in task 002. The PCF writes the typed `sprk_regarding{...}` lookups + the discriminator (its standard `applyResolverFields` / `PolymorphicResolverService` behavior) — giving the thread the same regarding-resolution `sprk_communication` already has, WITHOUT a second regarding mechanism (ADR-046 path-C: reuse the PCF, add a bindable Lookup).

    The thread regarding change (from the PCF write) is the trigger for the re-derive in (1). Keep the naming-edited marker + discriminator writes ADDITIVE (NFR-04 — the existing Text `sprk_regardingrecordtype` is NOT retyped and stays the denormalized copy). This is BFF (`BuildTopic` re-derive + marker read) + PCF config (0 code); `/conflict-check` before the PR (shared resolver file, after 070).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF + PCF integrator for the Communication subsystem. Authority on `Services/Communication/ThreadResolver.cs` and on the entity-agnostic RegardingResolver PCF placement pattern. Fluent in ADR-046 (no second regarding mechanism — reuse RegardingResolver + a bindable Lookup), ADR-024 (11-entity regarding family mirrored by `RegardingFieldMap.All`), ADR-028 (read path untouched), §10 BFF Hygiene, §11 Component Justification. You add the smallest marker-gated re-derive to the resolver and place a shipped PCF via form config — no new component.
  </role>

  <goal>
    `ThreadResolver.BuildTopic()` re-derives `sprk_name` on a regarding change ONLY while the naming-edited marker (task 002) says "auto"; a user edit flips the marker to "edited" and is preserved on subsequent regarding changes. The existing RegardingResolver PCF is placed on the `sprk_communicationthread` form (`entity="sprk_communicationthread"`, 0 code) binding the new Lookup discriminator and writing the typed regarding lookups + discriminator. Both marker + discriminator writes are additive (NFR-04). Build clean; publish-size (≈0) + CVE + Placement Justification reported; Step 9.5 FULL gates run; `/conflict-check` clean before PR.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Task 002 adds to `sprk_communicationthread`: typed `sprk_regarding{...}` lookups (all 11, mirroring `RegardingFieldMap.All`), a NEW Lookup discriminator field, a naming-edited marker (boolean auto-vs-edited), and the default-thread marker (consumed by 070). This task consumes the naming-edited marker + the Lookup discriminator.

      Current naming: `ThreadResolver.CreateThreadAsync` sets `sprk_name = TruncateTo(BuildTopic(...), 200)` once at create (line 101). `BuildTopic` (line 175) prefers the message subject, then the anchor record name, then a channel-typed fallback ("Conversation" / "(No Subject)"). There is NO re-derive on regarding change and no auto-vs-edited flag — a user rename is silently clobbered if re-derive were added naively, which is exactly what the marker gate prevents.

      Regarding on the thread: R1 wrote only the denormalized regarding text quartet (`sprk_regardingrecordid/type/name/url`). The thread's `sprk_regardingrecordtype` is **Text** (not a Lookup), so RegardingResolver — which requires a Lookup binding — cannot attach until task 002 adds the Lookup discriminator. `sprk_communication`'s regarding is written server-side by the association engine; the THREAD's regarding is what this PCF resolves on the form.

      **Component Justification (§11):** no NEW component. The re-derive EXTENDS `BuildTopic` (existing method). RegardingResolver is REUSED via config (0 code — it is already entity-agnostic per FR-22). The only new surface (the naming-edited marker + Lookup discriminator) belongs to task 002. Cost-of-doing-nothing: without the marker gate, either the name never refreshes on a regarding change (stale thread names — Success Criterion 4 fails) OR a naive re-derive clobbers user edits (data loss); without the PCF placement + Lookup discriminator, thread regarding stays manual/denormalized and RegardingResolver cannot attach.

      **Scope discipline:** extend `BuildTopic`'s call path with a marker gate; place the PCF via form config. Do NOT modify RegardingResolver's code (0 code change). Do NOT add a second regarding mechanism (ADR-046 — no CommunicationConnections / Field Mapping Framework). Do NOT retype the Text `sprk_regardingrecordtype` (NFR-04). Do NOT touch the read path (ADR-028).
    </background>
