    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-07">Add "re-derive `sprk_name` unless user-edited" to `ThreadResolver.BuildTopic()` gated by the naming-edited marker; name re-derives on regarding change ONLY while the marker says "auto"; a user edit sets the marker to "edited" and is preserved. Place the existing RegardingResolver PCF (`entity="sprk_communicationthread"`, 0 code) on the thread form binding the new Lookup discriminator; it writes typed lookups + discriminator.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-06 / ADR-024">The typed `sprk_regarding{...}` lookups the PCF writes mirror `RegardingFieldMap.All` (all 11). The re-derive reads the thread's resolved regarding (the same ADR-024 family), not a new mechanism.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-046">Path-C comply — REUSE RegardingResolver (0 code) + a bindable Lookup discriminator (task 002). MUST NOT use CommunicationConnections PCF or the Field Mapping Framework for thread regarding; MUST NOT introduce a second regarding mechanism.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-04">The naming-edited marker + Lookup discriminator writes are ADDITIVE. MUST NOT retype the existing Text `sprk_regardingrecordtype` (breaking — ThreadResolver + membership + timeline filters still read it).</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-02">The re-derive path stays best-effort / non-fatal — a re-derive/marker read failure MUST NOT throw to the caller (log + keep the existing name).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028 / NFR-03">Write/resolve-side + form-config only. MUST NOT touch the impersonation read path or add any access logic.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Depends on 070 (same file, landed first). Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (shared `Services/Communication/` hot-path). RegardingResolver placement is form config on `sprk_communicationthread` — 0 PCF code change.</constraint>
