  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read `ThreadResolver.cs` (`BuildTopic` line 175, `CreateThreadAsync` line 95, `ReadRegardingAnchorAsync` line 128), the task-002 naming-edited marker + Lookup discriminator schema (exact field names + types), and the RegardingResolver manifest + `applyResolverFields` write behavior. Confirm the trigger: a regarding change on the thread (PCF write) is what should refresh the name.</step>
    <step order="2">Read `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` §F + root §11 + ADR-046 (path-C reuse) + ADR-024 + ADR-028 (read path untouched) before editing.</step>
    <step order="3">Implement the marker-gated re-derive: add a re-derive path that, on a thread regarding change while the naming-edited marker = "auto", re-runs `BuildTopic` and updates `sprk_name`; when the marker = "edited", leaves `sprk_name` untouched. Ensure the create path stamps the marker = "auto" initially. Keep the re-derive best-effort/non-fatal (NFR-02).</step>
    <step order="4">Define the marker flip: a user edit to `sprk_name` sets the marker to "edited". If the flip is enforced by a plugin/flow rather than the BFF, DOCUMENT the exact mechanism + where it lives in the PR/notes; if the BFF owns it on its write path, implement it there. State the chosen mechanism explicitly (root §6 — surface ambiguity rather than guessing).</step>
    <step order="5">Place the RegardingResolver PCF on the `sprk_communicationthread` main form: `entity="sprk_communicationthread"`, bound to the task-002 Lookup discriminator; verify it writes the typed `sprk_regarding{...}` lookups + discriminator (mirrors `sprk_communication`'s resolution). Confirm 0 RegardingResolver code change. Declare the bound field (per R1 lesson — a code component only appears in the form component library if it binds a field).</step>
    <step order="6">Confirm additivity (NFR-04): the marker + discriminator writes touch only the new task-002 fields; the Text `sprk_regardingrecordtype` is untouched and still the denormalized copy read by ThreadResolver/membership/timeline filters.</step>
    <step order="7">Write tests for the re-derive gate: (a) regarding change while marker=auto → `sprk_name` re-derives; (b) user edits name → marker=edited → a SUBSEQUENT regarding change PRESERVES the edited name; (c) a re-derive failure is non-fatal (NFR-02, existing name kept). Re-run 070's characterization + tier tests — confirm STILL GREEN (naming change does not disturb the ladder).</step>
    <step order="8">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` + the targeted ThreadResolver tests — all green.</step>
